WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.840
Avengers, assemble — for a funeral.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:06.759
According to a new rumor making the rounds,
a major character in the cast of Avengers:

00:00:06.759 --> 00:00:11.090
Infinity War will meet their maker in the
very first few moments of the movie, kicking

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.920
off the epic battle with a point for Thanos's
team.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.100
Citing "a reliable source", ScreenGeek has
published a report hinting at "the death of

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.580
a major Marvel character," and that the death
will have huge consequences, both in this

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.600
movie and the adventures to come.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.600
The source states:

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.990
"Some fans will be expecting it, while others
will be blindsided.

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:33.160
It sets the tone for the rest of the movie
— as well as the future of the MCU."

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.989
It's hard to respond to this news by doing
anything other than throwing out guesses.

00:00:36.989 --> 00:00:41.350
In response to the report, ScreenCrush drew
a connecting line between this news and a

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.860
previous quote from Marvel head Kevin Feige
at Brazil's Comic-Con, in which he stated

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:50.220
that Thanos would establish himself, quote,
"within the first five minutes" of the movie.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:56.540
"Thanos shows us why he's the biggest, baddest
villain we've ever had."

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:00.379
There aren't too many candidates that fit
the framework other than Loki, the trickster

00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:04.969
god who was last seen at the end of Thor:
Ragnarok standing side-by-side with his brother

00:01:04.969 --> 00:01:07.450
as they encountered Thanos's massive ship.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:11.689
While we don't know exactly what happens after
the sons of Odin meet Thanos, we do know that

00:01:11.689 --> 00:01:15.950
Thor makes it out of the encounter alive,
sailing through space to encounter the Guardians

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:16.950
of the Galaxy.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.240
So… where's Loki?

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.439
Avengers: Infinity War will be out in theaters
worldwide on April 27th.

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:27.399
Until then, be wary of decoy spoilers that
may circulate to preserve the movie's twist.

00:01:27.399 --> 00:01:29.409
Remember: Thanos demands your silence.

00:01:29.409 --> 00:01:32.900
We're almost there, folks — fingers crossed
that your favorite character makes it out

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:33.900
alive.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.299
As the ScreenGeek source said,

00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:39.249
"It's good that the Russo Brothers are telling
fans to be emotionally prepared for the film

00:01:39.249 --> 00:01:41.359
— because they'll definitely need to be.

00:01:41.359 --> 00:01:44.289
Whether you're expecting it or not, it's going
to be big."

00:01:44.289 --> 00:01:45.299
Thanks for watching!

00:01:45.299 --> 00:01:47.969
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:01:47.969 --> 00:01:50.419
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

